{"id": "201376", "revid": "132185", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=201376", "title": "Curup", "text": "Curup is the capital city of Rejang Lebong regancy in Bengkulu.\nUnderstand.\nLandscape.\nCurup is a landlocked area, surrounded by Bukit Barisan on almost all sides. This vast expanse is known locally as \"luak\". Musi River also flow through the \"luak\".\nPeople.\nThe original inhabitants of this region are the Rejang (Tun Jang) tribe. As time goes by, people from other region came here. Immigrant races with significant populations are Javanese, Minangnese, Chinese, Serawainese, Lembaknese, Sundanese and various races from South Sumatra.\nFlora and fauna.\nThis area is also known as the habitat of Rafflesia arnoldii.\nTalk.\nThe native language spoken in Curup is Rejang language. But Malay language is increasingly used by people here.\nEat and drink.\nYou can find a lot of street foods (and beverages) near Jendral Sudirman and Ahmad Yani streets.\nSleep.\nDespite the name, hotels in this city are basically guest houses."}
